---
// Figure: the user who made a change sees it, with a recent-write marker.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="inv-marker" title="The person who made the change sees it" controls="steps"
  caption="A sequence of steps, not a timed simulation. The half-second invalidation delay stands for any delay between the commit and the delete: a relay, a change stream or a replica. The marker's ten seconds must exceed that delay.">
  <Choice slot="params" name="marker" label="After the write, the application" value="plain"
    options={[{ value: 'plain', label: 'does nothing more' }, { value: 'marker', label: 'sets a recent-write marker' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>Doing nothing more: Sam renames themselves Samira and the change commits, but the relay's delete reaches Redis half a second later. The page reloads straight away and gets the cached profile, Sam. The delete then arrives, too late for the one person who was looking.</p>
    <p>With a marker: straight after the commit the application sets recent-write:user:7 for ten seconds. On the reload it finds the marker, skips the cached profile for this user and reads Samira from the database. The relay's delete arrives as usual, and when the marker expires the user reads from the cache again.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { switchSequence } from './switch-sequence.mjs';
  import { markerSpecs } from './sequences.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="inv-marker"]').forEach(root => switchSequence(root, markerSpecs, 'marker'));
</script>
